---
/**
 * Security camera installation, San Antonio.
 *
 * Kelly, 2026-10-25: "We do cameras and it pays well. If we can get some of this business, I'd like
 * that." Search Console that day: about 30th on average for "security camera installation san
 * antonio" (Google Ads: about 90 a month, 390 in September 2026), 0 clicks in 28 days. Page one was
 * Google Maps listings, an AI answer built from them, and thin pages (a tag page, Facebook answers,
 * directories). This rebuild adds the licensing answer, the cost answer, wired vs Wi-Fi, FAQ schema
 * and links to the cost page.
 * Prices come from src/data/camera-prices.ts (Kelly approved 2026-11-05); the sentences here match it.
 * Still needed from Kelly: real camera job photos for the hero. License B-15669: Kelly, 2026-10-26.
 *
 * Wired first (Kelly, 2026-11-05): "Wired is best but if there is no way to wire them, we do WiFi cams."
 * The two lead questions are real people's words: Facebook "San Antonio - Ask A Local" titles Google showed
 * for "security camera installation san antonio", San Antonio, 2026-11-05 (kz/website/faq-source-log.md).
 *
 * Ring block (Kelly, 2026-10-26: "add a ring section please"). "ring doorbell installation" draws about
 * 50 San Antonio searches a month, 90 in December (Google Ads tool, 2026-10-26). KZ quotes Ring
 * Spotlight Cams with Ring solar panels (Hye Springs Ranch proposal, 2026-10-26). Ring facts from
 * ring.com support, read 2026-10-26: saved video needs a Ring plan (live view and alerts are free);
 * each wired doorbell needs a transformer rated for it, and Ring sends transformer work to an
 * electrician, so the copy says we check it, not that we replace it. No price: none is set for Ring.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../../components/sections/HeroSection.astro';
import TrustBar from '../../components/sections/TrustBar.astro';
import TestimonialsSection from '../../components/sections/TestimonialsSection.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/sections/FAQAccordion.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/sections/CTASection.astro';
import LowVoltageFirst from '../../components/sections/LowVoltageFirst.astro';
import CameraPrices from '../../components/sections/CameraPrices.astro';
import { ALY_BEYNON, ANDRES_PEREZ, ZACK_CROFT } from '../../data/reviews';

const PAGE_URL = 'https://kzaudioandvideo.com/security-camera-installation-san-antonio/';
const COST_URL = '/security-camera-installation-cost-san-antonio/';

const faqs = [
  {
    // Facebook, San Antonio - Ask A Local, shown by Google 2026-11-05: "Who installs hardwired security cameras in San Antonio".
    question: 'Who installs hardwired security cameras in San Antonio?',
    answer: 'KZ Audio & Video does. Wired is the best way to do cameras, so we run a network cable to every camera and back to a recorder in your home whenever there is a way to run it. If there is truly no way to wire a spot, we put a WiFi camera there. We hold Texas Private Security Board license B-15669, and our own crew does the work. Call or text (210) 981-4098.',
  },
  {
    // Facebook, San Antonio - Ask A Local, shown by Google 2026-11-05: "Who installs self-monitored home security cameras in San" (title cut off by Google).
    question: 'Who installs self-monitored home security cameras in San Antonio?',
    answer: 'KZ Audio & Video installs them. A self-monitored system records to a recorder in your home with no monthly monitoring fee, and sends live video and motion alerts to your phone. We set up the app and show you how to use it before we leave. Call or text (210) 981-4098.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What types of security cameras do you install?',
    // Brands per Kelly, 2026-10-25: "We do Illumavue, alibi and ubiquiti" (maker spells it Illumivue).
    answer: 'We install wired and wireless indoor and outdoor security cameras from Illumivue, Alibi and Ubiquiti (UniFi Protect). We also install doorbell cameras, including Ring video doorbells and Ring cameras, and integrate camera systems with existing home technology setups. Wired is best: more reliable, less susceptible to interference, and not relying on Wi-Fi coverage. It is what we install whenever there is a way to run the cable. If there is no way to wire a spot, we use a WiFi camera there.',
  },
  {
    // Google "People also ask" on "security camera installation san antonio", 2026-10-25.
    question: 'Do you need WiFi for a surveillance camera?',
    answer: 'Not if the cameras are wired. A wired PoE (Power over Ethernet) camera gets its power and its data over one network cable run back to the recorder, so it keeps recording even when your Wi-Fi drops. You only need internet to watch from your phone when you are away from home. Wireless cameras do depend on Wi-Fi signal, plus batteries or a nearby outlet, which is why we recommend wired PoE for any system you want to trust.',
  },
  {
    // Google "People also ask" on "low voltage contractor san antonio", 2026-10-25.
    question: 'Do you need a license to do low voltage work in Texas?',
    answer: 'It depends on the work. Texas\'s electrician licensing law exempts most low voltage wiring, such as speaker, TV and network cable (Texas Occupations Code 1305.003). Security is different: a camera system that records counts as an alarm system under Texas Occupations Code 1702.002, so installing one for someone else takes a license from the Texas Private Security Board, part of the Department of Public Safety. KZ Audio & Video holds that license, number B-15669.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I monitor my cameras remotely from my phone?',
    answer: 'Yes. Every system we install includes remote access: you can view live feeds, review recorded footage, and receive motion notifications from your iOS or Android device. We configure the app, walk you through it, and make sure you know how to use it before we leave.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How many cameras do I need for my home?',
    answer: 'Most residential installs run four to twelve cameras covering main entry points, driveways, garages, backyards, and side yards. We assess your property and coverage goals and recommend the minimum number that gives you real coverage, not an upsell to cameras you don\'t need.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you integrate cameras with home automation systems?',
    answer: 'Yes. We can integrate camera feeds with existing home automation platforms and tie into your existing network infrastructure. If you have a smart home system already, we work with it. If you\'re building new, we design the camera system alongside your AV and low voltage installation.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you install cameras in new construction?',
    answer: 'Yes, new construction is ideal for camera installation because we can run wiring before the walls are closed. We work with custom home builders across San Antonio and the Hill Country and coordinate camera pre-wire alongside all other low voltage work.',
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Security Camera Installation",
  "serviceType": "Security camera installation",
  "url": PAGE_URL,
  "description": "Licensed security camera installation in San Antonio TX: wired 4K PoE cameras, local NVR recording, Ring and other doorbell cameras and phone access, designed around a home's real entry points.",
  "provider": { "@type": "HomeAndConstructionBusiness", "@id": "https://kzaudioandvideo.com/#business", "name": "KZ Audio & Video" },
  "areaServed": ["San Antonio", "Stone Oak", "Alamo Heights", "Helotes", "Boerne", "Bulverde", "Fair Oaks Ranch", "Timberwood Park", "New Braunfels", "Canyon Lake"].map((name) => ({ "@type": "City", "name": `${name}, TX` })),
  "offers": {
    "@type": "AggregateOffer",
    "priceCurrency": "USD",
    "lowPrice": "700",
    "highPrice": "13100",
    "url": `https://kzaudioandvideo.com${COST_URL}`
  }
};

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": faqs.map(({ question, answer }) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": question,
    "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": answer }
  }))
};

const breadcrumb = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://kzaudioandvideo.com" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Security Camera Installation San Antonio" }
  ]
};

const featured = ALY_BEYNON;
const secondary = [ZACK_CROFT, ANDRES_PEREZ];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Licensed Security Camera Installation San Antonio | KZ"
  description="Licensed security camera installation in San Antonio. Wired 4K PoE cameras, local NVR recording, Ring doorbells, phone access. From $2,200. Call (210) 981-4098."
  schema={[schema, faqSchema, breadcrumb]}
>

  <HeroSection
    overline="Security Cameras · Licensed in Texas · Since 1999"
    heading="Security Camera Installation in San Antonio TX"
    subhead="Wired camera systems designed around your home's real entry points, recorded on-site, and on your phone. KZ Audio & Video is licensed by the Texas Private Security Board (B-15669) and has run low voltage in San Antonio since 1999."
    ctaLabel="See Camera Prices"
    ctaHref={COST_URL}
    secondaryCta="Or call: (210) 981-4098"
    secondaryHref="tel:2109814098"
    imageSrc="/images/projects/young-theater/stone-oak-theater-left-speaker-wire.jpg"
    imageAlt="Low voltage cable run to a wall box at framing, before drywall, in a custom home"
    imagePosition="object-center"
  />

  <TrustBar />

  <!-- Self-contained answer, written to be quoted. Prices match the cost page. -->
  <section id="hardwired-security-cameras" class="section bg-charcoal">
    <div class="container-main">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-start">
        <div class="lg:col-span-7">
          <p class="overline mb-3">The Short Answer</p>
          <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-6">Who Installs Hardwired Security Cameras in San Antonio?</h2>
          <p class="text-body-lg text-stone leading-relaxed">
            KZ Audio & Video installs hardwired security cameras in homes across San Antonio and the Texas Hill Country. Wired is the best way to do cameras, so it is what we install whenever there is a way to run the cable. Each camera gets one network cable back to a recorder in your home. That cable carries its power and its video, so it keeps recording when the Wi-Fi drops and there are no batteries to change. Your footage stays on your own recorder with no monthly monitoring fee, and you watch it from your phone. If there is truly no way to wire a spot, we put a WiFi camera there and test the signal first. KZ Audio & Video holds Texas Private Security Board license B-15669, and our own crew runs the cable, mounts the cameras and sets up the app. At KZ, five to eight wired 4K cameras with a recorder run $3,300 to $6,200 installed. Call or text (210) 981-4098.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-5 card p-7">
          <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-h4 text-warm-white mb-4">How we decide: wired or WiFi</h3>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            {[
              'New home: the camera cable goes in before the walls close.',
              'Finished home: we run the cable through the attic and walls first.',
              'No way to wire a spot: a WiFi camera goes there, with the signal tested first.',
            ].map((q) => (
              <li class="flex gap-3 text-body-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">
                <svg class="flex-shrink-0 mt-1 text-gold" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg>
                <span>{q}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <a href={COST_URL} class="btn-text text-sm cursor-pointer inline-block mt-6">See camera prices &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Self-contained answer, written to be quoted. Numbers match the cost page. -->
  <section class="section bg-slate-surface">
    <div class="container-main">
      <p class="overline mb-3">The Short Answer</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-6">What Does Security Camera Installation Cost in San Antonio?</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-stone max-w-3xl leading-relaxed mb-10">
        At KZ Audio & Video, a wired security camera system in San Antonio typically costs $2,200 to $12,300 installed, depending on how many cameras you need and how the cable gets there. Three to four wired 4K cameras with a recorder run $2,200 to $3,700. Five to eight run $3,300 to $6,200, and nine to sixteen run $6,000 to $12,300. The recorder (an NVR) means there is no monthly fee. As a planning number, that is about $600 to $900 per wired camera, counting the camera, cable, mounting, setup and its share of the recorder. If there is truly no way to wire a spot, a WiFi camera runs about $335 with a solar panel. A sharper low-light camera adds $275 each, and a dual-lens zoom camera is $1,900 each plus cable and install. We walk the property, find the real entry points, and give you a written quote.
      </p>
      <CameraPrices />
      <a href={COST_URL} class="text-gold text-body font-medium hover:text-warm-white transition-colors cursor-pointer">Full price breakdown and estimate calculator &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Services -->
  <section class="section bg-charcoal">
    <div class="container-main">
      <p class="overline mb-3">Camera Systems</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-6">
        Professional Installation. Remote Access. No Guesswork.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-stone mb-12 max-w-2xl">
        Consumer camera systems are easy to install yourself. Professional camera systems: properly positioned, wired, and configured, are a different category. We install systems that give you real coverage and remote access that actually works.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        {[
          { title: 'Outdoor Cameras', desc: 'Weather-resistant cameras covering driveways, entries, garages, side yards, and backyards. Properly aimed, properly lit, properly wired.' },
          { title: 'Indoor Cameras', desc: 'Interior cameras for entry points, common areas, and any space you want visibility into. Discreet mounting, clean installation.' },
          { title: 'Wired NVR Systems', desc: 'Network video recorder systems with local storage and remote access. More reliable than cloud-only systems. Footage stored on-site.' },
          { title: 'Doorbell Cameras', desc: 'Video doorbell installation, Ring included, wired for reliability, with remote access and motion notifications to your phone.' },
          { title: 'New Construction Pre-Wire', desc: 'Camera wire runs at rough-in stage in new construction. Coordinate alongside AV and low voltage for a complete installation.' },
          { title: 'Home Automation Integration', desc: 'Camera systems integrated with existing home automation and smart home platforms. One app, full visibility.' },
        ].map(({ title, desc }) => (
          <div class="card p-7 flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-h4 text-warm-white">{title}</h3>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">{desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Licensing and wired vs wireless -->
  <section class="section bg-slate-surface">
    <div class="container-main">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
        <div>
          <p class="overline mb-3">Licensed in Texas</p>
          <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-6">Does a Camera Installer in Texas Need a License?</h2>
          <p class="text-body-lg text-stone leading-relaxed mb-5">
            Yes, for a system that records. Texas law counts a camera system that records images of a home or business as an alarm system (Texas Occupations Code 1702.002), so installing one for someone else takes a license from the Texas Private Security Board, part of the Department of Public Safety.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body text-stone leading-relaxed">
            KZ Audio & Video holds that license, number B-15669, and the same crew runs the cable, mounts the cameras and sets up the recorder. Ask any installer you are considering for theirs.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="overline mb-3">Wired or Wireless</p>
          <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-6">Wired Is Best. WiFi Only When There Is No Way to Wire.</h2>
          <p class="text-body-lg text-stone leading-relaxed mb-5">
            A PoE camera gets power and data over one network cable back to the recorder. It records continuously, it does not drop when the Wi-Fi does, and there are no batteries to change.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body text-stone leading-relaxed">
            That is why wired is what we install whenever there is a way to run the cable, in new homes and finished homes alike. If there is truly no way to wire a spot, we put a WiFi camera there and test the signal first. Building a home? Our <a href="/new-construction-prewire-guide/" class="text-gold hover:text-warm-white transition-colors underline underline-offset-2 cursor-pointer">New Construction Prewire Guide</a> shows where the camera cable goes before drywall. Running UniFi at home? See our <a href="/unifi-installer-san-antonio/" class="text-gold hover:text-warm-white transition-colors underline underline-offset-2 cursor-pointer">UniFi installer page</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Ring. Inside this section so the page keeps its slate and charcoal alternation. -->
      <div id="ring" class="mt-16 pt-16 border-t border-smoke/60 scroll-mt-28">
        <p class="overline mb-3">Ring Doorbells and Cameras</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-6">Do You Install Ring Doorbells and Cameras?</h2>
        <p class="text-body-lg text-stone max-w-3xl leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Yes. We install Ring video doorbells and Ring cameras in San Antonio homes, and we set up the Ring app on your phone before we leave. A wired Ring doorbell runs on the home's existing doorbell wire and transformer, so there is no battery to charge. Each wired model needs a transformer rated for it, so we check yours before we mount anything and tell you up front if it falls short. Battery Ring cameras, like the Ring Spotlight Cam, need no wiring, and a Ring solar panel keeps them charged. Most Ring devices send video over Wi-Fi, so the signal where each one mounts matters: we check it first and fix the network when it needs it. Live view and alerts are free in the Ring app. Saving and replaying video takes a paid Ring plan.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body text-stone max-w-3xl leading-relaxed mb-10">
          Want everything recorded at home with no monthly fee? That is what a wired PoE system with a local recorder does, and we install both.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <article class="card p-7 flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-h4 text-warm-white">Ring Video Doorbells</h3>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">Mounted on your existing doorbell wire, with the transformer checked first and the app set up on your phone.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card p-7 flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-h4 text-warm-white">Ring Spotlight Cams</h3>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">Aimed at the driveway, side yard or back gate, with a Ring solar panel on battery models so nobody climbs a ladder to charge them.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card p-7 flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-h4 text-warm-white">Strong Wi-Fi Where Ring Records</h3>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">We test the signal at every spot before we mount, and fix weak Wi-Fi with a proper <a href="/home-network-installation-san-antonio/" class="text-gold hover:text-warm-white transition-colors underline underline-offset-2 cursor-pointer">home network</a>.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <TestimonialsSection featured={featured} secondary={secondary} />

  <LowVoltageFirst
    heading="Low Voltage First, Then the Cameras"
    rough="A network cable to every camera location, home-run to the recorder, plus the doorbell wire, all in place before the walls and soffits close."
    installs="We mount and aim the cameras, set up the recorder, and get the app working on your phone."
    existing="On a finished home we run the same camera cable through the attic and walls first, then mount the cameras."
  />

  <FAQAccordion
    heading="Security Camera Installation: Frequently Asked Questions"
    faqs={faqs}
  />

  <CTASection
    heading="Get Real Camera Coverage for Your Home"
    body="Book a free consultation. We'll assess your property, talk through coverage goals, and give you a quote, no pressure."
    ctaLabel="Book a Free Consultation"
    ctaHref="/contact-kz-audio-video-san-antonio-tx/"
    secondaryLabel="Call (210) 981-4098"
    secondaryHref="tel:2109814098"
  />

</BaseLayout>
